<title>UK: GEC shares gain on British submarine order.</title>
<headline>GEC shares gain on British submarine order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Electric Co Plc added six pence to 389 after defence sources here said late on Thursday that Britain will give GEC Marconi a two billion pound order for three nuclear-powered submarines.</p>
<p>The sources said the Trafalgar class submarines would be built at GEC's VSEL Barrow shipyard.</p>
<p>A GEC spokesman declined to comment as long as no official announcement had been made.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
